---
description: Backend/FastAPI/SQLite rules for HADES
globs:
  - "backend/**/*.py"
alwaysApply: false
---
- Keep API contracts explicit and typed with Pydantic where practical.
- SQLite writes must be transactional; migrations must preserve existing user data.
- Do not move deterministic policy/permission decisions into model prompts.
- Long work must be bounded, cancellable and persist progress/checkpoints when applicable.
- Convert blocking filesystem/subprocess/network work off the async event loop.
- Do not swallow failures that affect correctness; persist/return structured failure state.
- Add a regression test for every fixed backend bug.
